PREFACE 
 
The Population and Housing Census (PHC)  2021 was taken on the 6 th of November 2021. It 
was the 11th census conducted by the Samoa Bureau of Statistics since Samoa gained 
Independence on January 1st 1962. This is the first census that the Computer Assisted Personal 
Interview (CAPI) method was used to collect information compared to the use of Paper and 
Pencil Interview (PAPI) method in previous census es. This is the second report published for 
the Populatio n and Housing Census 2021. In the previous censuses, analytical reports were 
prepared, however the users especially students found it too technical for their purposes and we 
have changed our approach by preparing the basic tables in this document and a sep arate Fact 
sheet in which the high -level indicators collected by the census  are provided in a very simple 
way. The next series of reports using the census dataset will include the 51districts profiles, the 
disability, gender and youth  monographs. Additional information will also be made available 
upon request, on any particular dataset, based on the information collected in the 2021 census. 
We encourage planners, policy-makers, the business es, non- governmental organizations and 
the community at large to  make good use of these data for decision making and to formulate 
relevant policies that would further improve the social and economic developments for Samoa. 
 
The PHC 2021 is one memorable activity since it implemented during the year of the outbreak 
of the deadly disease  the COVID 19 pandemic and the sudden passing away of the former 
Government Statistician Ms Aliimuamua Malaefono Taua Faasalaina Taaloga and these lead 
to the delay in some of the census planned activities. 
 
The census was funded by the Government of Samoa with financial assistance by the UNFPA. 
The Bureau also acknowledged with much appreciation the support provided by the people  
of  Samoa especially in providing information that have been part of the survey. Finally, I 
commend the Management and staff who have been actively involved in the conduct of the 
Population and Housing Census 2021.  
 
IA SAGA FAAMANUIA LE ALII -FAAFETAI. 
 
 
Leota Aliielua Salani 
Government Statistician/CEO 

 
