Note:  
The sex ratio is the number of males per 100 females. 
 
The dependency ratio is a measure showing the number of dependents, aged 0-14 and age 65years and over, to the total working age population of 15-64. It is 
also referred to as the "total dependency ratio"  
 
People with disability categorize as compilation of two level of difficulties - a lot of difficulties and cannot do at all specified as disability 
 
The median age is the age that divides a population into two numerically equal groups. i.e., half the population is younger than this age and half is older. 
 
Urban area refers to the Apia urban area (AUA) comprising of 4 political districts namely Vaimauga 2,3,4 and Faleata 1 while the rural area refers to the other 
3 remaining regions of North West Upolu (NWU), Rest of Upolu (ROU) and Savaii (SAV), comprising of the remaining 47 political districts. 
 
