EXECUTIVE SUMMARY 
 
 
On the 6th of Nov 2021, the Population of Samoa was 205,557 (51percent were male and 49percent 
were female) .The new count shows an increase of 9,578 people as compares to 195,979 recorded  in 
2016 census. Upolu Island   continues to have the bigger share of the total population which is 
78percent. The growth on Upolu island has been directed at North West Upolu region  (37percent) 
and less on the central Apia Urban Area region(18percent) . Faleata 1 is the most populated district 
(6percent) but Falealupo is the least populated district(0.4percent)  among the 51political districts. 
There are more males than females especially in the young age which gives a sex ratio of 104males to 
100 females, but when it comes to life expectancy , females are expected to live longer for 77years 
compares to  74years for males. The median or average age of the total population was 22years 
reflecting a young and youthful Samoan population .The youthful population indicated continuous 
demands for developments catering for the needs of the younger population such as education, health 
and employment opportunities. 
Religion 
The Congregational Christian Church of Samoa (CCCS/EFKS) still the dominant religion in 
Samoa with 27% in 2021. This is followed by the Catholic Church (19%) the Latter Day Saints 
(18%), the Methodist (12%) , the Assembly of God (AOG) (10%)  and all other churches have been 
catching up with their share of attendants, as they all made up 16%  of the total church attendants in 
2021. 
Education 
 
The majority of the population aged 3years and above had ever attended the Secondary school level 
of year 9-13 (48percent).  The majority of population 15years and above had attained School 
Certificate or lower (36percent) as their highest qualification. 
 
Persons with disabilities 
 
Out of 177,788persons aged 5years and above interviewed   for disability questions, about 2.5percent 
of them had some form of disabilities. 
 
Household 
 
The majority of households in Samoa enumerated in the census 2021 were   private households with a 
total of   31,137 and 19households were institutional households and the average household size for 
private household   was 6.6. 
 
