INTRODUCTION
Taking of the Population and Housing Census 2021
The Census of Population and Housing is one of the important sources of statistical
information for planning and policy making purposes. It entails a great deal of
information relating to social, demographic and economic characteristics of the
whole population.
The census counted all persons who were present and been living in Samoa for at
least three months on census night (November 6
th 2021) excluding Samoans  who
were overseas for more than three months or visiting Samoa at the time for less than
three months. The census was coordinated by the Samoa Bureau of Statistics.
The Statistics Act 2015
The conduct of the Population and Housing Census 2021, was conducted pursuant
to Part II, Section 7 of the Statistics Act 2015 , whereby the Samoa Bureau of
Statistics (SBS) is required to conduct the census of population and housing every
five years, to meet national data needs of all stakeholders or to conduct the census
at any other time as seen fit by the Minister of Statistics.  .
Preparation and financial assistance
The total cost of the PHC 2021 is amounted to ST1, 803,560.00.  The Government
of Samoa funded the activity with financial assistance of around ST 100, 000
from the UNPFA, which supported census publicity and awareness programs.
Publicity and census awareness
The publicity of the census 2021 theme “Everyone counts” or “E taua ma faitau
tagata uma” in the Samoan language started in October 2020 up unt

